NOTICE
======

What the CC0 dedication in LICENSE covers, and what it cannot.

This repository builds https://rockenhaus.net/, a public archive of filed court
documents in two Michigan divorce cases. It is dedicated CC0 1.0 Universal.

A dedication can only be made by someone who holds the rights being dedicated.
This one is written to be precise about that, because a repo-wide LICENSE with
no scoping asserts a dedication over material the dedicator does not hold, and a
downstream reuser relying on it inherits the gap.


CC0 APPLIES TO
--------------

  * the site's source: templates, stylesheets, build scripts, tests
  * documents authored by Conrad Alan Rockenhaus, including his own filings
  * data this project derived from the record: the text extracted from the PDFs
    under _corpus/, the generated manifests, citations.json, and the answer
    pages built from them

For the derived data, the dedication also clears database-right ambiguity for
reusers in jurisdictions that recognise one.


CC0 CANNOT APPLY TO
-------------------

  * DOCUMENTS AUTHORED BY OTHER PARTIES. Filing a document with a court does not
    transfer its copyright. Motions, responses and correspondence authored by
    another party remain their author's work. They are reproduced here as public
    court records; that reproduction does not, and cannot, dedicate them.

  * THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL INSIDE EXHIBITS. Screenshots, emails and documents
    created by people who are not parties to these cases remain their authors'
    work, whatever exhibit they appear in.

Their authors' rights are unaffected by anything in LICENSE.


COURT ORDERS ARE A SEPARATE CASE
--------------------------------

Orders and opinions written by judges in their judicial capacity are not subject
to copyright at all, so no dedication is needed or possible for them. They are
free to reuse because of what they are, not because of this file.


WHAT THIS MEANS IF YOU ARE REUSING THIS MATERIAL
------------------------------------------------

Take the code, the extracted text and the derived data freely; that is what the
dedication is for, and mirroring is expected.

For the filed documents themselves, you are reusing public court records, which
carries its own considerations that this file does not attempt to resolve for
you. What it does tell you is which parts of this repository this project is in
a position to dedicate, and which it is not.


ON PERMANENCE
-------------

CC0 is irrevocable and mirror-friendly by design. If a court later seals a
document, this site can comply and remove it; mirrors cannot be recalled. Every
publication decision here is therefore permanent in practice, which is why the
build refuses to publish content carrying protected personal identifiers rather
than relying on removing it afterwards. See scripts/check_pii.py.
